      "name": "memory_write",
    },
    {
      "description": "Drafts a message (email, chat message or text) for the user to send. Work out the situation (a work disagreement, negotiating, following up, bad news, asking, setting a boundary, apologising, declining, feedback, cold outreach, delegating, celebrating) and what is at stake in the relationship.

When it is high-stakes, ambiguous or has competing goals, give 2 or 3 variants that lead to different outcomes, not just different tones, each labelled by its goal ("Disagree and commit" vs "Push for alignment", "Gentle nudge" vs "Create urgency"). When it is transactional or needs only wording help, give one. Emails get a subject line. Match the channel: emails longer and more formal, chat short, texts brief.

The card shows each draft in full with copy and open buttons, so do not repeat the drafts in your reply; add at most a sentence or two on how the variants differ or what to adjust.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "kind": {
            "description": "'email' shows a subject and an open-in-mail button; 'textMessage' an open-in-messages button; 'other' neither.",
            "enum": [
              "email",
              "textMessage",
              "other",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "summary_title": {
            "description": "A short title for the message.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "variants": {
            "description": "The drafts, one per approach.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "body": {
                  "description": "The message.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "label": {
                  "description": "2 to 4 word goal-oriented label: 'Hold firm', 'Suggest alternative', 'Polite decline'.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "subject": {
                  "description": "Email subject (only for kind 'email').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "label",
                "body",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "kind",
          "variants",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "message_compose_v1",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a set of distinct approaches the user could take, each with concrete next steps. Use it for personal health questions where the answer is 2 to 6 alternatives ("what can I do about mild knee pain"). Every option needs a one or two sentence description and at least two actionable bullets.

Do not use it for one nuanced recommendation, for options that need explaining more than doing, for an A-vs-B comparison, for a diagnosis question, or outside health.

Keep bullets to one short line. The card carries its own not-medical-advice note: do not add a disclaimer, and do not list the options again in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "options": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "bullets": {
                  "description": "Concrete next steps, one short line each. At least two.",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 8,
                  "minItems": 2,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "description": {
                  "description": "One or two sentences on what it is and when it helps. Do not restate the bullets.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "title": {
                  "description": "Name of the option (a few words).",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "title",
                "description",
                "bullets",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 8,
            "minItems": 2,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "Short heading for the set (one line).",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "options",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "options_card_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a list of places, each with photos and a short description. Use it when the answer is a set of 2 to 8 specific places to visit (cafes, hikes, neighbourhoods, hotels) and photos help ("good ramen spots in Shibuya", "best beaches near Lisbon"). Only for places you found by web search or already know.

Do not use it for a day-by-day plan (itinerary_display_v0) or a single place (write it in text).

Pass each place's name and description; photos are added from the names, so never pass image URLs. A description can run to a paragraph: what it is like, what to order or do, when to go. Do not list the places again in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "places": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "description": {
                  "description": "Optional. What to do or expect there.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "name": {
                  "description": "Name of the place (a few words).",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "tips": {
                  "description": "Optional. Up to three very short (2 to 4 word) labels: 'Book ahead', 'Go for sunset'.",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 3,
                  "type": "array",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 8,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "places",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "places_list_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Gives files to the user as file cards; a Markdown, HTML, React (.jsx), Mermaid, SVG or PDF file also opens beside the chat as an artifact. Use it for every file the user should get, after it is created; not for intermediate files you only read yourself. A file outside output/ is copied there first. Put the file the user should open first at the front of the list.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "filepaths": {
            "description": "Paths of the files to give the user.",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "filepaths",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "present_files",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows products one per page, each with photos, name, price and a short blurb. Use it for shopping questions where the user wants to look at a handful of recommendations one at a time ("walk me through 3 good espresso machines", "show me a few standing desks").

Do not use it for a single best pick (featured_card_display_v0), for named options weighed on shared criteria (comparison_card_display_v0), or when the blurb would only restate the name or it is not something to buy.

Each blurb can run to a paragraph: why it fits and its trade-offs. Do not list the products again in your text. Photos are added for you: never pass image URLs.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "products": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "blurb": {
                  "description": "Up to a paragraph on why it fits and its trade-offs. Do not restate the name or price.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "name": {
                  "description": "Product name (a few words).",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "price": {
                  "description": "Display price with currency, e.g. '$549'. Omit when not applicable or unknown.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "url": {
                  "description": "Absolute https URL of the product page. Omit when you do not have a real one; never make one up.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 6,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "products",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "product_carousel_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows an interactive multiple-choice quiz as a card; the same questions can be flipped through as flashcards (question on the front, answer and explanation on the back). Use it when the user asks for a quiz, practice questions or a self-test, including on documents or notes they shared. Each question needs plausible wrong answers, a short explanation of why the right one is right, and optionally a hint. Default to 5 questions unless asked for a number. Give each question its own short correct_feedback and incorrect_feedback labels when you can; defaults cover any that lack them.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "description": {
            "description": "Optional one line on what it covers.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "initial_mode": {
            "description": "Which view opens first: 'quiz' (default, graded one at a time) or 'flashcards', for review or memorising rather than testing: use it when the user asks for flashcards or to study or review. The user can switch either way.",
            "enum": [
              "quiz",
              "flashcards",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "questions": {
            "description": "The questions, in order.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "correct_feedback": {
                  "description": "Optional short bold label for a right answer ('Exactly!'): a few words in the question's language, ending with a full stop or exclamation mark. Vary it across questions and match the tone of the quiz.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "correct_option_id": {
                  "description": "The correct option's id; must be one of this question's option ids.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "explanation": {
                  "description": "Why the correct answer is right, shown after answering.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "hint": {
                  "description": "Optional hint shown on request, nudging without giving the answer away.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "id": {
                  "description": "Unique id within the quiz ('q1').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "incorrect_feedback": {
                  "description": "Optional short bold label for a wrong answer ('Not quite.'): a few words in the question's language, ending with a full stop or exclamation mark. Encouraging, never mocking; vary it across questions.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "options": {
                  "description": "The answer choices, at least 2, in a natural order.",
                  "items": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "id": {
                        "description": "Short id within the question ('a').",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                      "text": {
                        "description": "The answer text.",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "id",
                      "text",
                    ],
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "minItems": 2,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "prompt": {
                  "description": "The question.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "question_type": {
                  "description": "Only multiple_choice.",
                  "enum": [
                    "multiple_choice",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "id",
                "question_type",
                "prompt",
                "options",
                "correct_option_id",
                "explanation",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short phrase (under 45 characters) naming what the card holds ('5-question quiz on photosynthesis'), with no full stop: it is shown as a compact label. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "Quiz title ('Photosynthesis basics').",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "questions",
          "summary",
          "title",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "quiz_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Opens a past chat at a conversation_search hit and returns the turns around it. Not for reading whole chats.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "conversation_id": {
            "description": "The chat id from a tool result. Never guess one.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "max_turns": {
            "description": "Turns to return, up to 50. Defaults to 20.",
            "maximum": 50,
            "minimum": 1,
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "page_token": {
            "description": "A hit's page_token, or next_page_token / prev_page_token. Omit to start at the beginning.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "conversation_id",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "read_conversation",
    },
    {
      "description": "Returns what show_widget needs: the theme's CSS variables and colours, typography, layout rules and examples for a kind of visual. Call it before your first show_widget call, and again later for a different module. It is a setup step: do not mention or narrate it; go straight on to the visual.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "modules": {
            "description": "Which modules to load. Pick all that fit.",
            "items": {
              "enum": [
                "diagram",
                "mockup",
                "interactive",
                "data_viz",
                "art",
                "chart",
                "elicitation",
              ],
              "type": "string",
            },
            "type": "array",
          },
          "platform": {
            "description": "'mobile' when the person is on a narrow (~380px) screen, so sizes suit it; otherwise 'desktop'. Defaults to 'unknown' (desktop sizing).",
            "enum": [
              "mobile",
              "desktop",
              "unknown",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "read_me",
    },
    {
      "description": "Lists the user's most recently updated chats (inside a project, that project's), newest first, with a short excerpt of each. Page with before and after.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "after": {
            "description": "Only chats updated after this ISO date-time.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "before": {
            "description": "Only chats updated before this ISO date-time.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "n": {
            "description": "How many chats, 1 to 20. Defaults to 3.",
            "maximum": 20,
            "minimum": 1,
            "type": "integer",
          },
        },
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "recent_chats",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows an interactive recipe whose servings the user can change, scaling every amount. Use it when the user asks for a recipe, cooking instructions or how to prepare a dish.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "base_servings": {
            "description": "Servings at the given amounts. Defaults to 4.",
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "description": {
            "description": "Optional short description.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "ingredients": {
            "description": "The ingredients with amounts.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "amount": {
                  "description": "The quantity at base_servings.",
                  "type": "number",
                },
                "id": {
                  "description": "4-character id referenced from steps ('0001').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "name": {
                  "description": "Display name; put a counting noun here for whole items ('garlic cloves', 'large eggs').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "unit": {
                  "description": "Omit for whole items. Give seasonings a real starting amount in tsp.",
                  "enum": [
                    "g",
                    "kg",
                    "ml",
                    "l",
                    "tsp",
                    "tbsp",
                    "cup",
                    "fl_oz",
                    "oz",
                    "lb",
                    "pinch",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "amount",
                "id",
                "name",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "type": "array",
          },
          "notes": {
            "description": "Optional tips or variations.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "steps": {
            "description": "The instructions. Write {ingredient_id} to show an ingredient's scaled amount inline.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "content": {
                  "description": "The full instruction, e.g. 'Whisk {0001} and {0002}'.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "id": {
                  "description": "Unique id for the step.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "timer_seconds": {
                  "description": "Seconds, for any step that involves waiting (cooking, baking, resting, chilling). Omit for hands-on steps.",
                  "type": "integer",
                },
                "title": {
                  "description": "Short summary ('Boil pasta'); also the timer label.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "content",
                "id",
                "title",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "type": "array",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "The dish ('Spaghetti alla carbonara').",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "ingredients",
          "steps",
          "title",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "recipe_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows visual content inline alongside your reply: SVG graphics and diagrams, charts, or interactive HTML widgets. Use it for flowcharts, architecture diagrams, dashboards, forms, calculators, data tables, games, illustrations or any visual. Code starting with <svg is drawn as SVG, anything else as HTML. A global sendPrompt(text) puts a follow-up in the person's message box for them to send. Call read_me before your first show_widget call, silently, then answer as if you went straight to the visual.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "loading_messages": {
            "description": "1 to 4 messages of about 5 words shown while the visual draws, in the person's language. One for a simple visual, more for a complex one. On a serious topic (illness, disease, pandemics, death, grief, war, conflict, poverty, disaster, trauma, abuse, addiction, medical decisions, politically charged subjects, or anything the reader may be personally affected by) keep them plain: describe what the code is doing in the dullest generic words, with no drama ("Setting up the model", not "Charting the battle ahead"). If you have to ask whether a topic is serious, it is. Otherwise they can be playful.",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
            },
            "maxItems": 4,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "Short snake_case name for this visual, specific enough to tell it apart from the conversation's other visuals ('q4_revenue_by_product_line', not 'chart'). Also the download file name: no spaces or special characters.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "widget_code": {
            "description": "The SVG or HTML to draw. SVG: raw code starting with <svg>, colours from the CSS variables. HTML: content only, no DOCTYPE, <html>, <head> or <body>. Use the CSS variables for theming, keep the background transparent and avoid top-level padding. Scripts run after the code is complete.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "loading_messages",
