      "name": "chart_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows 2 or 3 products side by side, with attribute rows lined up. Use it for shopping questions weighing a few named options on the same criteria ("iPad Air vs iPad Pro", "compare these three monitors").

Do not use it for one product (featured_card_display_v0) or more than three (product_carousel_display_v0); when the options share no comparable attributes; when the user wants one recommendation with reasoning; or for approaches or plans rather than things to buy.

Use the same attribute labels in the same order for every product so the rows line up. Do not repeat the products or values in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "products": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "attributes": {
                  "items": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "label": {
                        "description": "Short attribute name ('Display', 'Battery'). The same labels, in the same order, for every product.",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                      "value": {
                        "description": "This product's value for the attribute.",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "label",
                      "value",
                    ],
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 8,
                  "minItems": 2,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "name": {
                  "description": "Product or option name (a few words).",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "price": {
                  "description": "Display price with currency, e.g. '$1,099'. Omit when not applicable or unknown.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "url": {
                  "description": "Absolute https URL of the product page. Omit when you do not have a real one; never make one up.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
                "attributes",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 3,
            "minItems": 2,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "products",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "comparison_card_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows your single best product pick as one rich card: name, optional price, and why it is the pick. Use it for shopping questions with one clear answer ("the best entry-level espresso machine", "just tell me which one to get").

Do not use it when the user wants several to browse (product_carousel_display_v0), is weighing named options on shared criteria (comparison_card_display_v0), or when the blurb would only restate the name or it is not something to buy.

The blurb can run to a paragraph: why this is the pick and its trade-offs. Do not describe the product again in your text. Photos are added for you: never pass image URLs.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "products": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "blurb": {
                  "description": "Up to a paragraph on why it fits and its trade-offs. Do not restate the name or price.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "name": {
                  "description": "Product name (a few words).",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "price": {
                  "description": "Display price with currency, e.g. '$549'. Omit when not applicable or unknown.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "url": {
                  "description": "Absolute https URL of the product page. Omit when you do not have a real one; never make one up.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 1,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "products",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "featured_card_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a day-by-day trip with a tab per day and the stops of each day. Use it for trip planning where the answer is an ordered schedule over one or more days, each with at least one named stop ("3 days in Lisbon", "plan a weekend in Kyoto").

Do not use it for a single place or a flat list of places with no days (places_list_display_v0); for more than 7 days or more than 12 stops in a day (summarise in text); for general travel advice (visas, packing, budget); or when the stops have no meaningful order.

Keep each blurb to one short line and day labels under about 12 characters. Do not list the itinerary again in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "days": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "day_label": {
                  "description": "Tab label: 'Day 1', 'Sat 14 Jun'. Under 12 characters.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "stops": {
                  "items": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "blurb": {
                        "description": "Optional. One short line on what to do or expect.",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                      "name": {
                        "description": "The place or activity (a few words).",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                      "time": {
                        "description": "Optional. A time or a rough slot ('9:00 AM', 'Afternoon').",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "name",
                    ],
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 12,
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "type": "array",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "day_label",
                "stops",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 7,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "Short heading for the trip ('3 days in Tokyo'). One line.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "days",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "itinerary_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows 1 to 6 web links as preview cards with title, site and an optional snippet. Use it for outside pages the user should open: search results, citations or further reading that back your answer ("find me articles on X", "where can I read more").

Do not use it for content in the chat itself, for one incidental link (put it in the text), for more than six (pick the best six), or for any entry without a real absolute http(s) URL: never make up a link; drop that entry.

Keep titles to one line and snippets to one or two sentences. Do not list the URLs again in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "links": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "domain": {
                  "description": "Optional site name ('Wirecutter'). Taken from the URL when omitted.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "snippet": {
                  "description": "Optional one or two sentences on why the link is relevant.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "title": {
                  "description": "Page title (one line, under about 80 characters).",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "url": {
                  "description": "Absolute http(s) URL the card opens.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "url",
                "title",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 6,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "links",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "link_preview_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Drafts a message (email, chat message or text) for the user to send. Work out the situation (a work disagreement, negotiating, following up, bad news, asking, setting a boundary, apologising, declining, feedback, cold outreach, delegating, celebrating) and what is at stake in the relationship.

When it is high-stakes, ambiguous or has competing goals, give 2 or 3 variants that lead to different outcomes, not just different tones, each labelled by its goal ("Disagree and commit" vs "Push for alignment", "Gentle nudge" vs "Create urgency"). When it is transactional or needs only wording help, give one. Emails get a subject line. Match the channel: emails longer and more formal, chat short, texts brief.

The card shows each draft in full with copy and open buttons, so do not repeat the drafts in your reply; add at most a sentence or two on how the variants differ or what to adjust.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "kind": {
            "description": "'email' shows a subject and an open-in-mail button; 'textMessage' an open-in-messages button; 'other' neither.",
            "enum": [
              "email",
              "textMessage",
              "other",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "summary_title": {
            "description": "A short title for the message.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "variants": {
            "description": "The drafts, one per approach.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "body": {
                  "description": "The message.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "label": {
                  "description": "2 to 4 word goal-oriented label: 'Hold firm', 'Suggest alternative', 'Polite decline'.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "subject": {
                  "description": "Email subject (only for kind 'email').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "label",
                "body",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "kind",
          "variants",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "message_compose_v1",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a set of distinct approaches the user could take, each with concrete next steps. Use it for personal health questions where the answer is 2 to 6 alternatives ("what can I do about mild knee pain"). Every option needs a one or two sentence description and at least two actionable bullets.

Do not use it for one nuanced recommendation, for options that need explaining more than doing, for an A-vs-B comparison, for a diagnosis question, or outside health.

Keep bullets to one short line. The card carries its own not-medical-advice note: do not add a disclaimer, and do not list the options again in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "options": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "bullets": {
                  "description": "Concrete next steps, one short line each. At least two.",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 8,
                  "minItems": 2,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "description": {
                  "description": "One or two sentences on what it is and when it helps. Do not restate the bullets.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "title": {
                  "description": "Name of the option (a few words).",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "title",
                "description",
                "bullets",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 8,
            "minItems": 2,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "Short heading for the set (one line).",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "options",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "options_card_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a list of places, each with photos and a short description. Use it when the answer is a set of 2 to 8 specific places to visit (cafes, hikes, neighbourhoods, hotels) and photos help ("good ramen spots in Shibuya", "best beaches near Lisbon"). Only for places you found by web search or already know.

Do not use it for a day-by-day plan (itinerary_display_v0) or a single place (write it in text).

Pass each place's name and description; photos are added from the names, so never pass image URLs. A description can run to a paragraph: what it is like, what to order or do, when to go. Do not list the places again in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
