    {
      "description": "Shows an interactive multiple-choice quiz as a card; the same questions can be flipped through as flashcards (question on the front, answer and explanation on the back). Use it when the user asks for a quiz, practice questions or a self-test, including on documents or notes they shared. Each question needs plausible wrong answers, a short explanation of why the right one is right, and optionally a hint. Default to 5 questions unless asked for a number. Give each question its own short correct_feedback and incorrect_feedback labels when you can; defaults cover any that lack them.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "description": {
            "description": "Optional one line on what it covers.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "initial_mode": {
            "description": "Which view opens first: 'quiz' (default, graded one at a time) or 'flashcards', for review or memorising rather than testing: use it when the user asks for flashcards or to study or review. The user can switch either way.",
            "enum": [
              "quiz",
              "flashcards",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "questions": {
            "description": "The questions, in order.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "correct_feedback": {
                  "description": "Optional short bold label for a right answer ('Exactly!'): a few words in the question's language, ending with a full stop or exclamation mark. Vary it across questions and match the tone of the quiz.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "correct_option_id": {
                  "description": "The correct option's id; must be one of this question's option ids.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "explanation": {
                  "description": "Why the correct answer is right, shown after answering.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "hint": {
                  "description": "Optional hint shown on request, nudging without giving the answer away.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "id": {
                  "description": "Unique id within the quiz ('q1').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "incorrect_feedback": {
                  "description": "Optional short bold label for a wrong answer ('Not quite.'): a few words in the question's language, ending with a full stop or exclamation mark. Encouraging, never mocking; vary it across questions.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "options": {
                  "description": "The answer choices, at least 2, in a natural order.",
                  "items": {
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "properties": {
                      "id": {
                        "description": "Short id within the question ('a').",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                      "text": {
                        "description": "The answer text.",
                        "type": "string",
                      },
                    },
                    "required": [
                      "id",
                      "text",
                    ],
                    "type": "object",
                  },
                  "minItems": 2,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "prompt": {
                  "description": "The question.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "question_type": {
                  "description": "Only multiple_choice.",
                  "enum": [
                    "multiple_choice",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "id",
                "question_type",
                "prompt",
                "options",
                "correct_option_id",
                "explanation",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short phrase (under 45 characters) naming what the card holds ('5-question quiz on photosynthesis'), with no full stop: it is shown as a compact label. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "Quiz title ('Photosynthesis basics').",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "questions",
          "summary",
          "title",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "quiz_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows an interactive recipe whose servings the user can change, scaling every amount. Use it when the user asks for a recipe, cooking instructions or how to prepare a dish.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "base_servings": {
            "description": "Servings at the given amounts. Defaults to 4.",
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "description": {
            "description": "Optional short description.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "ingredients": {
            "description": "The ingredients with amounts.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "amount": {
                  "description": "The quantity at base_servings.",
                  "type": "number",
                },
                "id": {
                  "description": "4-character id referenced from steps ('0001').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "name": {
                  "description": "Display name; put a counting noun here for whole items ('garlic cloves', 'large eggs').",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "unit": {
                  "description": "Omit for whole items. Give seasonings a real starting amount in tsp.",
                  "enum": [
                    "g",
                    "kg",
                    "ml",
                    "l",
                    "tsp",
                    "tbsp",
                    "cup",
                    "fl_oz",
                    "oz",
                    "lb",
                    "pinch",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "amount",
                "id",
                "name",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "type": "array",
          },
          "notes": {
            "description": "Optional tips or variations.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "steps": {
            "description": "The instructions. Write {ingredient_id} to show an ingredient's scaled amount inline.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "content": {
                  "description": "The full instruction, e.g. 'Whisk {0001} and {0002}'.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "id": {
                  "description": "Unique id for the step.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "timer_seconds": {
                  "description": "Seconds, for any step that involves waiting (cooking, baking, resting, chilling). Omit for hands-on steps.",
                  "type": "integer",
                },
                "title": {
                  "description": "Short summary ('Boil pasta'); also the timer label.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "content",
                "id",
                "title",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "type": "array",
          },
          "title": {
            "description": "The dish ('Spaghetti alla carbonara').",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "ingredients",
          "steps",
          "title",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "recipe_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a numbered walkthrough for fixing or setting something up. Use it for how-to and tech-support questions answered in 3 to 8 ordered steps, each with a short title and a description ("reset my router", "set up two-factor on GitHub").

Do not use it for a single step or setting, for advice or background that is not a procedure, for choices between options, when order does not matter or steps would be filler, or for coding tasks where the user wants the code.

Step titles are a few imperative words, without "Step 1:"; a description can be a short paragraph, enough to do the step without guessing. Do not list the steps again in your text.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "steps": {
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "description": {
                  "description": "How to do it and why, enough to follow without guessing.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "title": {
                  "description": "The step in a few imperative words.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "title",
                "description",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 8,
            "minItems": 2,
            "type": "array",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "view": {
            "description": "'stepper' (default) shows one step at a time, for steps done in order; 'list' shows all at once.",
            "enum": [
              "stepper",
              "list",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "steps",
          "summary",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "step_card_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a translation card when the user asks how to say, write or translate a short passage (a message, sentence, phrase or a few lines) into another language: the original and the translation side by side, with copy and edit. Do not repeat the translation in your reply; afterwards add a sentence or two of nuance only (register, a regional note, what to change for another tone). Not for single-word lookups, long documents or files, or grammar explanations.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "pronunciation": {
            "description": "Romanisation (romaji, pinyin with tones) when the target script is not Latin.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "source_lang": {
            "description": "BCP-47 tag of the source ('en').",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "source_language": {
            "description": "The source language's name, in the conversation's language ('English').",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "source_text": {
            "description": "The text being translated, as the user gave it (lightly cleaned, no quotes).",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "summary": {
            "description": "One short sentence (under 15 words) naming what the card shows, read when the card cannot be drawn. Do not repeat the card's values. Write it last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "target_lang": {
            "description": "BCP-47 tag of the translation ('ja', 'es-MX').",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "target_language": {
            "description": "The target language's name, in the conversation's language, with region when it matters.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "translation": {
            "description": "The translation, in the register that fits. Plain text, no romanisation.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "source_language",
          "source_text",
          "summary",
          "target_lang",
          "target_language",
          "translation",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "translation_display_v0",
    },
    {
      "description": "Runs a bash command on a single-use sandbox computer: each call starts from an empty machine, so do the whole job in one command. No network access, and nothing can be installed: check that a library or program is there before relying on it. The files of the conversation are in input/ (read-only), at the path on each file's attachment line; a file already in your context needs no reading here. Write files for the user to output/ and hand them over with present_files. Output is truncated when long, so print summaries, not whole tables.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "command": {
            "description": "The bash command to run.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "description": {
            "description": "Why this command is being run.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "command",
          "description",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "bash_tool",
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows a text file with numbered lines, an image (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP) as a picture, or a directory listing two levels deep (hidden files left out). The line prefix (spaces, number, tab) is display only: never include it in str_replace. A text file with no view_range is cut in the middle past 16,000 characters. Skills are read from /skills/<name>/SKILL.md.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "description": {
            "description": "Why this is being viewed.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "path": {
            "description": "Path of the file or directory, e.g. "input/report.pdf" or "/skills/xlsx/SKILL.md".",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "view_range": {
            "description": "Optional [start_line, end_line] for a text file, from 1; [start_line, -1] reads to the end.",
            "items": {
              "type": "integer",
            },
            "maxItems": 2,
            "minItems": 2,
            "type": "array",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "description",
          "path",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "view",
    },
    {
      "description": "Creates a new file with the given content, making its folders. Fails when the path already exists: edit an existing file with str_replace, or overwrite it with bash_tool.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "description": {
            "description": "Why this file is being created. Give this first.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "file_text": {
            "description": "The whole content of the file. Give this last.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "path": {
            "description": "Path of the file to create. Give this second.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "description",
          "path",
          "file_text",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "create_file",
    },
    {
      "description": "Replaces one string in a file with another. old_str must match the file exactly and occur exactly once; widen it with surrounding text until it is unique. View the file just before editing it: after an edit, earlier views of that file are stale. input/ and /skills are read-only.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "description": {
            "description": "Why this edit is being made.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "new_str": {
            "description": "The replacement; empty deletes old_str.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "old_str": {
            "description": "The text to replace; it must occur exactly once.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "path": {
            "description": "Path of the file to edit.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "path",
          "description",
          "old_str",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "str_replace",
    },
    {
      "description": "Gives files to the user as file cards; a Markdown, HTML, React (.jsx), Mermaid, SVG or PDF file also opens beside the chat as an artifact. Use it for every file the user should get, after it is created; not for intermediate files you only read yourself. A file outside output/ is copied there first. Put the file the user should open first at the front of the list.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "filepaths": {
            "description": "Paths of the files to give the user.",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "filepaths",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "present_files",
    },
    {
      "description": "Lexical keyword search over the current project's indexed files. Returns the most relevant excerpts, not whole documents, ranked by BM25 term overlap — this is keyword matching, not semantic or conceptual search, so exact terms matter more than phrasing. Use it when the question likely depends on project-specific content that hasn't already appeared in this conversation. Do not use it for general-knowledge questions unrelated to the project.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "limit": {
            "description": "Maximum number of excerpts to return. Defaults to 5.",
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "query": {
            "description": "Keywords to search for, not a full natural-language question.",
            "type": "string",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "query",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "search_project_files",
    },
    {
      "description": "Reads the indexed text of one project file by id, starting at an optional cursor, for when a search excerpt is not enough context. The response is bounded and may be truncated — check \`truncated\` and pass the returned \`nextCursor\` back in a follow-up call to continue reading. Only call this with a fileId already seen in this conversation, such as one returned by search_project_files. Do not guess a fileId.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "cursor": {
            "description": "Opaque cursor from a previous call's nextCursor. Omit to start from the beginning.",
            "type": "integer",
          },
          "fileId": {
            "description": "The file id, exactly as returned by search_project_files.",
            "type": "string",
          },
          "maxChars": {
            "description": "Soft budget for returned characters. The server enforces a hard cap regardless of this value.",
            "type": "integer",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "fileId",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "read_project_file",
    },
  ],
  "da5c9e6e7b8b5136": [
    {
      "description": "Shows tappable options to learn the person's preferences, constraints or goals before giving advice (a workout plan: goal, time, equipment; a book: genre, mood). Tapping is easier than typing on a phone.

First check the conversation: if the answer is already there or can be inferred, use it. If you are about to write clarifying questions as prose bullets, ask them with this tool instead.

Do not use it when the person asks "A or B?" (they want your recommendation), is venting, asks for your opinion, asks a factual question, needs written feedback, or already gave detailed constraints (proceed and state any assumption inline).

Always write a short message before the options. Prefer one question; three is a ceiling, not a target; each with 2 to 4 short, mutually exclusive options. Calling this ends your turn: the choice arrives as the person's next message, not as a tool result, so write nothing after it.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "questions": {
            "description": "1 to 3 questions to ask.",
            "items": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "options": {
                  "description": "2 to 4 options with short labels.",
                  "items": {
                    "description": "Short label.",
                    "type": "string",
                  },
                  "maxItems": 4,
                  "minItems": 2,
                  "type": "array",
                },
                "question": {
                  "description": "The question shown to the person.",
                  "type": "string",
                },
                "type": {
                  "description": "'single_select' to choose one option, 'multi_select' to choose one or more, 'rank_priorities' to drag the options into order. Defaults to single_select.",
                  "enum": [
                    "single_select",
                    "multi_select",
                    "rank_priorities",
                  ],
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "question",
                "options",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
            "maxItems": 3,
            "minItems": 1,
            "type": "array",
          },
        },
        "required": [
          "questions",
        ],
        "type": "object",
      },
      "name": "ask_user_input_v0",
    },
